# Page Object Model

One class per Sauce Demo screen under `com.automation.pages`, extending `BasePage`. Constructor is inherited; it assigns `driver = DriverFactory.getDriver()`. Do not pass `WebDriver` into page constructors.

## Required shape

```java
public class CartPage extends BasePage {
    private static final By CHECKOUT_BUTTON = By.id("checkout");

    public boolean isLoaded() {
        return isDisplayed(CART_LIST);
    }

    public CheckoutInfoPage clickCheckout() {
        click(CHECKOUT_BUTTON);
        WaitUtils.waitForUrlContains(driver, "checkout-step-one");
        return new CheckoutInfoPage();
    }
}
```

- `isLoaded()` on every page (existing pages already have it).
- Actions that stay on the same screen return `this` (`addProductToCart`, `fillInfo`, `sortBy`).
- Actions that change screens return the **next** page type (`loginSuccessfully` → `InventoryPage`).
- Split success vs error paths when the next page is not guaranteed: `login` vs `loginSuccessfully`; `continueCheckout` vs `continueCheckoutSuccessfully`.

## Assertions stay in tests

Pages expose state (`getErrorMessage`, `getCartItemNames`, `getCartBadgeCount`). Tests call `Assert.assertTrue` / `assertEquals`. Do not add TestNG asserts inside pages.

## Locators

Keep them private. Parameterized XPath is a private method, not a public locator:

```java
private By addToCartButtonFor(String productName) { /* InventoryPage pattern */ }
```

Do not duplicate `LoginPage` locators in `InventoryPage.logout` long-term — logout already uses `By.id("login-button")` inline; prefer `new LoginPage()` + `isLoaded()` in new code.

## New screens

If Sauce Demo grows, add `*Page.java` next to the existing six screens and wire returns into the page graph. Do not create a `components/` package for header/cart badge — those locators already live on `InventoryPage`.

## Missing

No Appium, no loadable-component library, no abstract `gotoUrl` on pages (`BaseTest` owns navigation to `baseUrl`).
